From e22f50c1663cdfaa1b9af63935afe6085bfdd8e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:49:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ss-delta: frame recorder; offline PSN entitlements for the
 add-ons (experimental, off)

* ctrl input pipe "record <count> <dir>": ss-delta.exe saves every
  rendered frame from the next one on, read back on the render thread
  (for glitches that last a few frames).
* NP auth HLE (NpState::entitlements): when enabled, sceNpAuthInit/
  CreateStartRequest/GetTicket/GetEntitlementIdList/GetEntitlementById
  answer from a local list. The ticket callback runs from the next
  sceNpCheckCallback, as on the system, since the game stores the request
  id first.
* ss-delta.exe [game] dlc (default false): reads the released add-ons
  from the game's resource/database/network/entitlement_table_us.csv in
  its archives (18 of 21 rows: the debug row and two never-released ones
  are left out) and starts the game's entitlement manager once
  (*(*0x81c9a4e0 + 0x44), as 0x818ca3c0 does). The game then holds all 18,
  but it hands add-ons out only from Cassus's Claim Gift page after an
  online "near" download step that does not complete offline. Not
  finished.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
